#: src/Privacy.php:47
msgid "Our photo galleries never store IP addresses or browser details, use no third-party analytics or tracking, and do not load anything from other websites."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:49
msgid "We count how often each gallery and photo is viewed, as anonymous daily totals. No cookie is set and nothing that identifies you is stored."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of days
#: src/Privacy.php:54
#, php-format
msgid "We keep it for %d days."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:55
msgid "We keep it until you ask us to delete it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:56
msgid "Some galleries ask for your email address before showing photos. We store the address you give, the gallery and the date, so we know who has seen the photos, and a cookie (slashphoto_email_…) remembers it in your browser for 30 days. If you are logged in, we note your account instead of asking."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:57
msgid "When you open a password-protected gallery, WordPress stores a cookie (wp-postpass) containing a scrambled form of the password, for up to 10 days."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:58
msgid "When you accept a gallery’s terms, a cookie (slashphoto_terms_…) remembers this in your browser for 30 days, and we record the acceptance with the date, which wording you accepted and your account or email address, so we can show what was agreed."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:59
msgid "When you open a gallery through a private link, a cookie (slashphoto_link_…) remembers this in your browser for 30 days. It contains only a signature of the gallery and the link; nothing about you is stored on our server."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:60
msgid "If you mark favourites without being logged in, they are kept only in your own browser (local storage) and never sent to us."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:61
msgid "If you choose images while logged in, we store your choice, any notes you write and the message you send with it, together with your account, so we can deliver your photos. It is deleted with your account or when we delete the gallery, and you can ask for a copy or for it to be erased."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:62
msgid "Your shopping cart is kept only in your own browser (local storage) until you order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Privacy.php:63
msgid "When you order, we store your name, email address, phone number if you give it, delivery address for prints, your message and what you bought, to deliver the order and for our bookkeeping. Orders that are never paid are deleted after a week. Paid orders are kept as long as accounting law requires."
